    delphi:hasConfidence "0.86"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Multi-trait pedigrees, genomic associations and selection experiments directly measure correlated response. Public livestock and crop data provide enough breadth for a strong present-day test, though not every selection regime." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Estimate genetic correlations and correlated responses between deliberately selected traits and unselected traits in breeding populations. Nonzero repeatable correlated responses support the claim; consistently independent traits would refute it." ;
